 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "c0a",
   "start": 2.2,
   "dur": 6.814263,
   "sub": "In this video, we'll install OpenCrabs on Ubuntu, from zero to your first chat. It takes about five minutes."
  },
  {
   "id": "c0b",
   "start": 9.564263,
   "dur": 9.687846,
   "sub": "You need Ubuntu 24.04 or newer on a 64-bit machine, an internet connection, and a key or subscription from an AI provider."
  },
  {
   "id": "c0c",
   "start": 19.802109,
   "dur": 4.937687,
   "sub": "Open a terminal. On the Ubuntu desktop, press Control, Alt and T."
  },
  {
   "id": "c1a",
   "start": 26.689796,
   "dur": 5.095261,
   "sub": "First, two quick checks. Your CPU type decides which file you download."
  },
  {
   "id": "c1b",
   "start": 32.335057,
   "dur": 10.834218,
   "sub": "x86_64 means you want the amd64 download. On an ARM machine you'll see aarch64 instead, and you want arm64."
  },
  {
   "id": "c1c",
   "start": 43.719274999999996,
   "dur": 5.861927,
   "sub": "Next, your glibc version. It must be 2.39 or newer."
  },
  {
   "id": "c1d",
   "start": 50.131201999999995,
   "dur": 9.567596,
   "sub": "Here it says 2.39, so we're good. Older than that? This download won't run there, so watch the older systems video instead."
  },
  {
   "id": "c2a",
   "start": 61.64879799999999,
   "dur": 10.603968,
   "sub": "Now install three small helpers. curl downloads files, jq reads the release info, and libgomp is a library OpenCrabs needs to run."
  },
  {
   "id": "c2b",
   "start": 72.80276599999999,
   "dur": 7.393379,
   "sub": "Ubuntu asks for your password. Nothing appears while you type it. That's normal. Type it and press Enter."
  },
  {
   "id": "c2c",
   "start": 80.74614499999998,
   "dur": 4.474467,
   "sub": "Ubuntu fetches the package lists, then installs the helpers."
  },
  {
   "id": "c2d",
   "start": 85.77061199999999,
   "dur": 3.333084,
   "sub": "When you're back at the prompt, the helpers are ready."
  },
  {
   "id": "c3a",
   "start": 91.05369599999999,
   "dur": 7.019138,
   "sub": "Next, ask GitHub for the newest release, and keep its version number in a variable called TAG."
  },
  {
   "id": "c3b",
   "start": 98.62283399999998,
   "dur": 6.577256,
   "sub": "Print it to check. If you see a version number, like v0.5.4, you're good."
  },
  {
   "id": "c3c",
   "start": 105.75008999999999,
   "dur": 5.201338,
   "sub": "If the line comes back empty, just run the TAG command again before you move on."
  },
  {
   "id": "c4a",
   "start": 112.901428,
   "dur": 6.839683,
   "sub": "Now download and unpack it in one line. The TAG variable fills in the version for you."
  },
  {
   "id": "c4b",
   "start": 120.29111099999999,
   "dur": 7.789751,
   "sub": "List the folder. You get two files: opencrabs itself, and rtk, a small helper it ships with."
  },
  {
   "id": "c4c",
   "start": 128.630862,
   "dur": 7.235147,
   "sub": "On an ARM machine, the one that said aarch64, swap amd64 for arm64 in the file name."
  },
  {
   "id": "c5a",
   "start": 137.81600900000004,
   "dur": 6.936009,
   "sub": "This step is optional, but it's a good habit. Download the archive and the published list of checksums."
  },
  {
   "id": "c5b",
   "start": 145.86600900000008,
   "dur": 6.717687,
   "sub": "Then let sha256sum compare them. OK means your file is exactly what was released."
  },
  {
   "id": "c5c",
   "start": 153.1336960000001,
   "dur": 2.782472,
   "sub": "Unpack this checked copy, and you're set."
  },
  {
   "id": "c6a",
   "start": 157.86616800000013,
   "dur": 7.481293,
   "sub": "Now move both files into a folder on your path, so you can run OpenCrabs from anywhere. No sudo needed."
  },
  {
   "id": "c6b",
   "start": 165.89746100000013,
   "dur": 1.572925,
   "sub": "Check that it works."
  },
  {
   "id": "c6c",
   "start": 168.02038600000014,
   "dur": 9.513515,
   "sub": "If your terminal says command not found, open a new terminal window and try again. Still not found? Run this export line, then try once more."
  },
  {
   "id": "c7a",
   "start": 179.48390100000017,
   "dur": 4.507551,
   "sub": "Time for the first run. Type opencrabs and press Enter."
  },
  {
   "id": "c7b",
   "start": 184.5414520000002,
   "dur": 6.224422,
   "sub": "The setup wizard opens. Choose QuickStart, the sensible defaults, and press Enter."
  },
  {
   "id": "c7c",
   "start": 191.3158740000002,
   "dur": 6.829932,
   "sub": "Home Base is where OpenCrabs keeps its files. The default is fine. Press Enter."
  },
  {
   "id": "c7d",
   "start": 198.69580600000023,
   "dur": 6.888345,
   "sub": "Brain Fuel is the important one. Pick your AI provider. We'll choose Anthropic."
  },
  {
   "id": "c7e",
   "start": 206.13415100000023,
   "dur": 9.304376,
   "sub": "Now paste your API key, or a setup token if you have a Claude subscription. It's hidden on screen. Never share your key with anyone."
  },
  {
   "id": "c7f",
   "start": 215.98852700000023,
   "dur": 4.797687,
   "sub": "Keep the default model, or pick another one, and press Enter."
  },
  {
   "id": "c7g",
   "start": 221.33621400000024,
   "dur": 6.901837,
   "sub": "Always On can keep OpenCrabs running in the background. Skip it for now. There's a separate video for that."
  },
  {
   "id": "c7h",
   "start": 228.78805100000025,
   "dur": 4.891587,
   "sub": "Vibe Check makes sure everything is wired up. All OK? Press Enter."
  },
  {
   "id": "c7i",
   "start": 234.22963800000025,
   "dur": 5.530227,
   "sub": "Make It Yours lets you tell OpenCrabs about yourself. Press Escape to skip it for now."
  },
  {
   "id": "c7j",
   "start": 240.30986500000026,
   "dur": 3.022721,
   "sub": "Setup complete. And you're in. Say hi."
  },
  {
   "id": "c7k",
   "start": 243.88258600000026,
   "dur": 6.819501,
   "sub": "It answers. Your reply will be different, but that's it. OpenCrabs is installed and running."
  },
  {
   "id": "c8a",
   "start": 252.65208700000028,
   "dur": 6.322426,
   "sub": "If something goes wrong, here are the three errors people hit most, and the fix for each."
  },
  {
   "id": "c8b",
   "start": 259.5245130000003,
   "dur": 9.840522,
   "sub": "GLIBC_2.39 not found means your system is too old for this download. Watch the older systems video instead."
  },
  {
   "id": "c8c",
   "start": 269.91503500000033,
   "dur": 7.195556,
   "sub": "libgomp.so.1: cannot open shared object file means the helpers are missing. Go back to chapter 2."
  },
  {
   "id": "c8d",
   "start": 277.66059100000035,
   "dur": 7.550794,
   "sub": "gzip: unexpected end of file means TAG was empty. Run chapter 3 again, then download again."
  },
  {
   "id": "c9a",
   "start": 287.16138500000034,
   "dur": 4.420227,
   "sub": "Every command from this video is in the description, ready to copy."
  },
  {
   "id": "c9b",
   "start": 292.13161200000036,
   "dur": 7.577846,
   "sub": "Next up: keep OpenCrabs running in the background, and connect it to Telegram so you can chat from your phone. See you there."
  }
